# MCP server documentation

`MCP.md` at the repository root is the public catalog of Favlo’s `POST /mcp` tools and `favlo://` resources.

When you add, remove, or rename a tool or resource, change tool parameters or defaults, change optional-task behavior, or change what generate tools return (links, inline media, task fields), update `MCP.md` in the same change.

`docs/serve.md` stays the listener note: transport, queue, preemption, logging, and client wiring. Do not duplicate the full tool tables there; add or adjust a single pointer to `MCP.md` if the serve note still names tools inline.

Do not document chat completion or OpenAI HTTP routes in `MCP.md`. Do not add HTTP `/v1/images`, `/v1/videos`, or `/v1/audio` routes to satisfy MCP clients.

Follow [documentation.mdc](documentation.mdc) for tone and placeholders.
